7ccb8ea5f1b9,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Ego,their parents,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,babama and mamasa (joking relatives),"babama, mamasa",/san_silberbauer_147_1981_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_147_1981_sv::The principles of congruency and of alternating generations are both conditionally negated by the fact that Ego has joking relationships both with his cross-cousins and with their parents.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_147_1981_sv:p,1346
842fdcf8dcee,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,FaBr,ego/any other !Kung,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,joking status carried by kin terms,,"/san_marshall_204_sv:p::/san_marshall_204_sv::The !Kung were apparently not always assiduous in teaching their children the exact biological position of their kinsmen (whether a given man was FaBr or MoBr, for instance), and a person would not always know why he applied a certain term to someone, but he would know that the term he used was proper, and he would know the proper joking status to observe;",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_204_sv:p,1158
b5e83d471398,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,FaFa,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,mixed,,!guma ↔ !gun!a,"/san_marshall_230_sv:p::/san_marshall_230_sv::In Figure 5, ego is named for his FaFa, C. His FaFa and FaMo term ego !guma. He reciprocates calling them !gun!a and tũn.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_230_sv:p,1257
ba958e84ba34,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,FaMo,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,,!guma,"/san_marshall_230_sv:p::/san_marshall_230_sv::In Figure 5, ego is named for his FaFa, C. His FaFa and FaMo term ego !guma.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_230_sv:p,1258
c6076f150036,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Gao,/Qui,person,person,joking_relationship,symmetric,!go,!go,/san_marshall_23_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_23_1957_sv::We know two men who used the term !go for each other because each of them had a brother named Dam.,0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_23_1957_sv:p,1266
c78f3484b0bb,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Grandparents,Grandchildren,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking partners; joking relationship; joking relationship (less restrained),,"/san_marshall_205_sv:p::/san_marshall_205_sv::To make blatantly insulting jokes with old people is not proper. The deference due to aged persons is expressed in the joking relationship by a moderate tone, and the joking relationship between an old person and a considerably younger one, especially between grandparents and grandchildren, becomes a cozy, friendly intimacy without the sexual emphasis. || /san_marshall_22_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_22_1957_sv::It is not thought proper to make blatant or insulting sexual jokes with old persons. The deference which is shown to aged persons is expressed by Kin Relationships moderation, and the joking relationship between an old person and a considerably younger person, especially between grandparents and grandchildren, becomes a cosy friendly intimacy without the sexual emphasis. || /san_silberbauer_143_1981_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_143_1981_sv::There is a gradation of decreasing reserve in joking relationships. Behavior toward one's grandparents lacks many of the restraints of relationships with one's parents but is less free than that between cross-cousins of the same sex and approximate age. || /san_silberbauer_68_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_68_sv::It is a feature of many cultures that a specially friendly or affectionate relationship exists between alternate generations. Among the G/wi, where Regulation Of Marriage these are joking partners, this serves the useful purpose of allowing the grandparents to act as a counterweight to the perhaps somewhat austere authority of the parents and also to explain the parents' point of view to the children on a more friendly basis.",0.912,0.95,4,4,/san_marshall_205_sv:p; /san_marshall_22_1957_sv:p; /san_silberbauer_143_1981_sv:p; /san_silberbauer_68_sv:p,1161;1251;1331;1382
b087b86187f3,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,HuFa,SoWi,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,mixed,,≠tum; /utsu,"/san_marshall_216_sv:p::/san_marshall_216_sv::A woman HuFa is ≠tum; she is SoWi to him, termed /utsu.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_216_sv:p,1220
b761f0bb055c,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Men,Men,group,group,joking_relationship,symmetric,Kin Relationships,,"/san_marshall_205_sv:p::/san_marshall_205_sv::Men accuse each other of having genital organs of excessive size or abnormal condition (castration or circumcision), or of being excessively preoccupied with sexual intercourse, unable to leave their wives long enough to go hunting. || /san_marshall_21_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_21_1957_sv::Men accuse each other of excessive preoccupation with sexual intercourse or of having genital organs of excessive size or abnormal condition (castration or circumcision).",0.75,0.9,2,2,/san_marshall_205_sv:p; /san_marshall_21_1957_sv:p,1162;1231
63e0fd685efd,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Men,Women,group,group,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship; joking relationships,,"/san_marshall_205_sv:p::/san_marshall_205_sv::Men accuse women with whom they may joke of being lazy, useless, slovenly, wanton, or ugly ... The women retaliate, perhaps accusing the men of being worthy only of castration or of unfaithful wives. Frequently a man joking with a woman calls her “my wife.” || /san_marshall_233_1961_sv:p::/san_marshall_233_1961_sv::Men and women must not speak openly together of sexual matters except as they make jokes in the joking relationship. || /san_marshall_235_1961_sv:p::/san_marshall_235_1961_sv::In view of this, the joking relationship has its interesting side. Men and women who have the joking relationship insult each other in a facetious way and also point out actual faults or remark on actual episodes which embarrass a person. || /san_marshall_290_sv:p::/san_marshall_290_sv::As far as we know, only two general subjects are avoided in conversation. Men and women do not discuss sexual matters openly together except as they make jokes in the joking relationships. || /san_marshall_294_sv:p::/san_marshall_294_sv::In view of this, the joking relationship has its interesting side. Men and women who have the joking relationship insult each other in a facetious way and also point out actual faults or remark on actual episodes which embarrass a person.",0.86,0.9,5,5,/san_marshall_205_sv:p; /san_marshall_233_1961_sv:p; /san_marshall_235_1961_sv:p; /san_marshall_290_sv:p; /san_marshall_294_sv:p,1163;1261;1262;1299;1300
ab18d5e68083,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Men,Women,group,group,joking_relationship,mixed,Kin Relationships,,"/san_marshall_21_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_21_1957_sv::Men accuse women with whom they may joke of being22 ugly, slovenly, or wanton. The women retaliate, perhaps accusing the men of being worthy only of castration or of unfaithful wives.",0.6,0.6,1,1,/san_marshall_21_1957_sv:p,1232
f584f1ad08e4,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,MoBr,ego/any other !Kung,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,joking status carried by kin terms,,"/san_marshall_204_sv:p::/san_marshall_204_sv::The !Kung were apparently not always assiduous in teaching their children the exact biological position of their kinsmen (whether a given man was FaBr or MoBr, for instance), and a person would not always know why he applied a certain term to someone, but he would know that the term he used was proper, and he would know the proper joking status to observe;",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_204_sv:p,1159
c65f2bead88e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,N/udukhwe,classificatory elder brother,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,,,/san_silberbauer_173_1981_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_173_1981_sv::N/udukhwe had shown restraint toward his classificatory elder brother by addressing his complaint to a third party and avoiding direct confrontation.,0.6,0.6,1,1,/san_silberbauer_173_1981_sv:p,1357
a0617562069e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Nunamiut,joking partners,ethnic group,group,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking partnership,,"/san_wiessner_355_1988_sv:p::/san_wiessner_355_1988_sv::If it is not possible for them to find a common relative other channels are still open—a name relationship, a dancing partnership, joking partnership, etc..",0.6,0.6,1,1,/san_wiessner_355_1988_sv:p,1418
121b51975583,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Parents,Offspring,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_339_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_339_1959_sv::About 18 inches is a minimum but is sufficient. The taboo is applied without sex differentiation: men must not sit near men or women, or women near women or men if they do not have the joking relationship. (3) With the exception of siblings of any age, the same persons who avoid joking avoid using each other's names in direct address. They use a kin term instead or the men may use a respect term for each other—!nau, ‘old man’. (4) Brothers and sisters do not sit near each other when they reach adolescence and, after marriage, when they have dwelling-places of their own, do not enter each other's scherms (shelters). (5) Parents and SoWi and DaHu, in addition to observing the joking, sitting, and name avoidances, do not enter each other's scherms and do not speak to each other in the first few years of their affinal relationship.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_339_1959_sv:p,1301
aeadebf1dd4b,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Parents and SoWi and DaHu,Children-in-Law,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,SoWi and DaHu,"/san_marshall_339_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_339_1959_sv::Parents-In-Law And Children-In-Law

...
(5) Parents and SoWi and DaHu, in addition to observing the joking, sitting, and name avoidances, do not enter each other's scherms and do not speak to each other in the first few years of their affinal relationship. They are the only persons in !Kung society who must avoid speaking together.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_339_1959_sv:p,1302
a8b16c8ef957,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,Parents-In-Law,Children-In-Law,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,speaking avoidance / avoidance of joking,,/san_marshall_251_sv:p::/san_marshall_251_sv::The speaking avoidance under these circumstances does not impose excessive inconvenience. ... The interactions of people who accord each other reserved behavior are not constrained in any way except in the avoidance of joking and the practice of the other avoidances just described.,0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_251_sv:p,1268
41377b47ac35,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,SiHu,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,reciprocal affinal terms / joking consistency,tũn!ga,"/san_marshall_216_sv:p::/san_marshall_216_sv::For example, a man terms his SiHu tũn!ga; to that man ego is WiBr, who is also termed tũn!ga.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_216_sv:p,1216
73d97e1400f0,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,WiBr,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,reciprocal affinal terms / joking consistency,tũn!ga,"/san_marshall_216_sv:p::/san_marshall_216_sv::For example, a man terms his SiHu tũn!ga; to that man ego is WiBr, who is also termed tũn!ga.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_216_sv:p,1217
78458ab5de08,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,WiFa,DaHu,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,≠tum,"/san_marshall_216_sv:p::/san_marshall_216_sv::A man terms his WiFa ≠tum; he is DaHu to that man, also termed ≠tum.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_216_sv:p,1219
9abf42695f47,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,WiSiHu,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,!go; tsĩ,"/san_marshall_216_sv:p::/san_marshall_216_sv::Ego and WiSiHu are !go and tsĩ to each other, and so forth.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_216_sv:p,1218
a2412f98e8e7,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,a boy,"babama (MB, FZH)",kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking kin,,"/san_silberbauer_151_1981_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_151_1981_sv::According to my informants, a boy would treat his babama (MB, FZH) and his ma:sa (fz, mbw) as avoidance kin as soon as he began to court their daughter, anticipating their conversion from joking kin to avoidance affines by the fact of his marrying their daughter.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_151_1981_sv:p,1348
a424356b21ae,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,a boy,"ma:sa (fz, mbw)",kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking kin,,"/san_silberbauer_151_1981_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_151_1981_sv::According to my informants, a boy would treat his babama (MB, FZH) and his ma:sa (fz, mbw) as avoidance kin as soon as he began to court their daughter, anticipating their conversion from joking kin to avoidance affines by the fact of his marrying their daughter.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_151_1981_sv:p,1349
c1df75ad3ccf,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,a man,his brother,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,/san_marshall_207_sv:p::/san_marshall_207_sv::A man jokes with his brother and with his brother's wife.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_207_sv:p,1185
74514ff4d3f5,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,a man,his brother's wife,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,/san_marshall_207_sv:p::/san_marshall_207_sv::A man jokes with his brother and with his brother's wife.,0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_207_sv:p,1186
9ffa94abaf5a,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,a man,his sister,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_207_sv:p::/san_marshall_207_sv::He refrains from joking with his sister and his sister's husband, and so forth.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_207_sv:p,1187
840903efc01d,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,a man,his sister's husband,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_207_sv:p::/san_marshall_207_sv::He refrains from joking with his sister and his sister's husband, and so forth.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_207_sv:p,1188
d844d9619848,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,a young man,a girl,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking partners,,/san_silberbauer_65_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_65_sv::A young man and a girl who are joking partners and of the appropriate ages are considered potential marriage partners.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_65_sv:p,1375
4bb50c4399d7,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,a young woman,an older woman,age_set,age_set,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,,"/san_shostak_306_sv:p::/san_shostak_306_sv::Between two people who have a joking relationship, the following scene might transpire. A young woman walks into the village with a bright strand of beads around her neck. An older woman sees them and jokes, “Oh, those beads are already mine! Your past stinginess is going to be turned around today!”",0.7,0.7,1,1,/san_shostak_306_sv:p,1328
47d9f5cd6baa,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,adolescent boy,adult man,age_set,age_set,joking_relationship,symmetric,banter,,"/san_sugawara_200_1988_sv:p::/san_sugawara_200_1988_sv::Then an adolescent boy (Tabu:ka) who was lying near the open-air fire called jokingly to Hxara:, “≠Kai, Hxara:be”. Immediately, Hxara: approached and shook Tabu:ka roughly and even attempting to step on his head. Tabu:ka rolled about on the sand. crying “Stop it! Hxara:!” ... In spite of the violent way in which Hxara: treated Tabu:ka, both of them remained smiling.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_sugawara_200_1988_sv:p,1385
1aaba643da27,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,adolescent or pubescent boys (residents),adolescent or pubescent boys (visitors),age_set,age_set,joking_relationship,symmetric,play fighting / joking relation,//gaikari-ku,"/san_sugawara_187_1988_sv:p::/san_sugawara_187_1988_sv::The third type of bodily contact occurs in a distinctive pattern of interaction called //gaikari-ku. Typically, //gaikari-ku means the play fighting between adolescent or pubescent boys which is performed in a way similar to a boxing match, but the verbal exchange of jokes or quasi abuse is also referred to by the same term.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_sugawara_187_1988_sv:p,1384
68dc0b27b8e1,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,all kin,joking or avoidance categories,group,group,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking vs avoidance classification,,"/san_silberbauer_65_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_65_sv::All kin are in either the joking or the avoidance categories and the behaviour is reciprocal, i.e. if I am in a cousin's joking category, he is also in mine.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_silberbauer_65_sv:p,1380
d8fb5fe264ce,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,an uncle,the uncle's wife,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_207_sv:p::/san_marshall_207_sv::In other words, if ego refrains from joking with an uncle, he also refrains from joking with the uncle's wife.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_207_sv:p,1191
553c6b7264bb,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,appropriate kin,appropriate kin,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,za,"/san_lee_372_1972_sv:p::/san_lee_372_1972_sv::The third and final phase of conflict on the verbal level is za (“sexual insulting”). The za mode occupies the ambiguous position of being both the highest form of affectionate joking between appropriate kin in the

“joking relationship” and the deadliest affront leading directly to fighting.",0.7,0.7,1,1,/san_lee_372_1972_sv:p,1152
b6d785a9df56,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ba:bama,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking category,ba:bama,"/san_silberbauer_312_1972_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_312_1972_sv::The following kin are in the joking category: 
ba:bama (patri- or matrilateral grandfather, spouse's grandfathers, FSiH, MBr)",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_312_1972_sv:p,1367
69c327be5d38,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,babam and masi (grandparents),n!odim and n!odisi (grandchildren),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking category,,"/san_tanaka_105_sv:p::/san_tanaka_105_sv::Grandparents (babam and masi) and grandchildren (n!odim and n!odisi), separated from ego by one generation, enter into the joking category.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_tanaka_105_sv:p,1405
1249a98a56b6,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,band members,his joking partners,group,group,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,joking partners,,"/san_silberbauer_318_1972_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_318_1972_sv::If the expression of a band's decision against him does not mend an offender's ways and he is impenitent in the face of the barbed comments of his joking partners, he will eventually be eased out of the band by means of a public conspiracy to keep him on the wrong foot.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_silberbauer_318_1972_sv:p,1373
9b030c71755e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,bearers of ego's father's name,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,like father,,"/san_lee_357_1972_sv:p::/san_lee_357_1972_sv::This principle is extended widely, so that a person with ego's father's name is treated “like father,” bearers of ego's mother's name are “like mother,” and bearers of ego's siblings' names are “like brother and sister.”",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_lee_357_1972_sv:p,1145
6f39eee2c8c9,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,bearers of ego's mother's name,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,like mother,,"/san_lee_357_1972_sv:p::/san_lee_357_1972_sv::This principle is extended widely, so that a person with ego's father's name is treated “like father,” bearers of ego's mother's name are “like mother,” and bearers of ego's siblings' names are “like brother and sister.”",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_lee_357_1972_sv:p,1146
52fc3c5e03b5,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,bearers of ego's siblings' names,ego,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,like brother and sister,,"/san_lee_357_1972_sv:p::/san_lee_357_1972_sv::This principle is extended widely, so that a person with ego's father's name is treated “like father,” bearers of ego's mother's name are “like mother,” and bearers of ego's siblings' names are “like brother and sister.”",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_lee_357_1972_sv:p,1147
9892fee11933,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,brother,sister,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_246_sv:p::/san_marshall_246_sv::The familiar pronoun, a, is used in addressing any child, and is used between persons who have the joking relationship, regardless of disparities in age. It is also used between brother and sister until they grow up, when they change to the respectful pronoun.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_246_sv:p,1267
bf55ca8cbcf9,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,co-wives,co-wives,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,!kwi; tsĩ; !gun!a; !guma; !gwa di,"/san_marshall_263_sv:p::/san_marshall_263_sv::Marriage to the same man gives co-wives the joking relationship, and they do not observe the sitting or the name avoidance, though they may have observed those avoidances and may have avoided joking before marriage. Co-wives apply the kin terms !kwi or tsĩ (sister) to each other, or, if they have the same name, they apply the terms !gun!a and !guma.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_263_sv:p,1293
e34faee0091b,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,co-wives,each other (co-wives of the same man),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,!Kwi,"/san_marshall_346_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_346_1959_sv::Marriage to the same man gives co-wives the joking relationship, and they do not observe the sitting or the name avoidance, though they may have avoided each other before marriage.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_346_1959_sv:p,1322
2e5de1f6a4b1,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,collaterals,affinal kin,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,relationship of joking or respect,,"/san_wiessner_106_1994_sv:p::/san_wiessner_106_1994_sv::Standard !Kung kinship terms are structured by relative age and generation, and each term carries with it a relationship of joking or respect that delimits eligibility for marriage and a range of permitted behavior.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_wiessner_106_1994_sv:p,1411
8475cfd64ee3,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,cousins,cousins,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking allowed with cousins,,"/san_marshall_260_sv:p::/san_marshall_260_sv::I believe that the system's allowing joking with cousins, although it prohibits marriage with them, may mitigate the force of the incest taboo and accounts to some extent for the tolerance toward the breakers of this rule.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_260_sv:p,1287
bb509ac558d7,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,cousins,each other,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_258_sv:p::/san_marshall_258_sv::In no category is marriage allowed when joking is prohibited, but in two categories marriage is prohibited while joking is allowed, namely, among cousins and among the parents of offspring's spouse.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_258_sv:p,1281
27bc8696a00d,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,cross-cousins,their parents,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking category,,"/san_silberbauer_311_1972_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_311_1972_sv::There are some situations in which it does not operate, for example, both cross-cousins and their parents are in the joking category, but this is changed if ego marries his cross-cousin, in which case the latter's parents are transferred to the avoidance category.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_311_1972_sv:p,1366
c66f558ba07f,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,cross-cousins of the same sex and approximate age,ego (reciprocal dyadic partner),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,,/san_silberbauer_143_1981_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_143_1981_sv::There is a gradation of decreasing reserve in joking relationships. Behavior toward one's grandparents lacks many of the restraints of relationships with one's parents but is less free than that between cross-cousins of the same sex and approximate age. The last is ideally close and friendly.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_143_1981_sv:p,1330
cfd603cb6714,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,!gun!a,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,!gun!a (joking),!gun!a,"/san_marshall_221_sv:p::/san_marshall_221_sv::The terms !gun!a and tũn are applied to the persons with whom ego may joke, tsu and //ga to persons with whom he avoids joking.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_221_sv:p,1233
6834856b2f5f,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,!gun!a (or tũn!ga w.s.) and tũn,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,"!gun!a, tũn, tũn!ga",/san_marshall_213_sv:p::/san_marshall_213_sv::Ego applies the terms !gun!a (or tũn!ga w.s.) and tũn to persons in his own generation and in generations alternate to his own; he has the joking relationship with anyone to whom he applies these terms.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_213_sv:p,1213
a28948c59df8,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,//ga,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,//ga (avoidance),//ga,"/san_marshall_221_sv:p::/san_marshall_221_sv::The terms !gun!a and tũn are applied to the persons with whom ego may joke, tsu and //ga to persons with whom he avoids joking.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_221_sv:p,1236
b630dfa95d9e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,A,kin_role,person,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_208_sv:p::/san_marshall_208_sv::Joking is reciprocal; if ego jokes with A, A jokes with ego.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_208_sv:p,1192
544a6b49641d,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,BrWiMo,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Marriage with a SiHu (as second wife or if her SiHu is a widower) or a man's with a BrWi (if the death or divorce of the brother makes the marriage with BrWi possible) is highly appropriate, and the parents of these affines, therefore, seem to ego “like” his spouse's parents.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1272
4a6c41fcb64b,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,DaHuFa,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Among the affines ego must not marry are SoWiFa, DaHuFa, SoWiMo, DaHuMo. Marriage with one of these would turn ego's So and SoWi, Da and DaHu into stepbrothers and stepsisters, which would be most awkward.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1274
09fb1c6424b2,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,DaHuMo,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Among the affines ego must not marry are SoWiFa, DaHuFa, SoWiMo, DaHuMo. Marriage with one of these would turn ego's So and SoWi, Da and DaHu into stepbrothers and stepsisters, which would be most awkward.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1276
f260f740fa58,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,FaBr,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,,"/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_342_1959_sv::Throughout the whole system (except among remote name relatives), ego maintains the same joking status with both members of a married couple, for example, with FaBr and FaBrWi, WiSi and WiSiHu, &c.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p,1310
62dc0eb3c045,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,FaBrWi,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,,"/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_342_1959_sv::Throughout the whole system (except among remote name relatives), ego maintains the same joking status with both members of a married couple, for example, with FaBr and FaBrWi, WiSi and WiSiHu, &c.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p,1311
40a9ffc6dd62,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,HuBrSo,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Why, we had asked, is marriage with WiSiDa and HuBrSo specifically prohibited? ≠Toma explained that a man often marries his WiSi if his wife should die, or as a second wife.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1270
807978994541,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,HuSi,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Marriage is prohibited with HuSiHu and WiBrWi, termed respectively ≠tum and / utsu; ego avoids joking with them as he avoids joking with HuSi and WiBr.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1279
0379f06f984b,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,HuSiHu,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,≠tum,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Marriage is prohibited with HuSiHu and WiBrWi, termed respectively ≠tum and / utsu; ego avoids joking with them as he avoids joking with HuSi and WiBr.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1277
d960aa9ec7c0,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,HuSiHu,person,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,avoidance / constrained from joking,,"/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_342_1959_sv::In the sibling category among affines ego is prohibited from marrying only WiBrWi or HuSiHu. ... As we list ego's siblings and affines in Fig. 4 we see that WiBrWi and HuSiHu are the only ones whose sex is opposite to ego's, making marriage possible, but with whom ego is constrained from joking because he does not joke with his WiBr or HuSi, according the same joking status to both members of a married couple.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p,1314
db817f9993ab,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,SiHuFa,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Marriage with a SiHu (as second wife or if her SiHu is a widower) or a man's with a BrWi (if the death or divorce of the brother makes the marriage with BrWi possible) is highly appropriate, and the parents of these affines, therefore, seem to ego “like” his spouse's parents.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1271
75546b5720eb,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,SoWiFa,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Among the affines ego must not marry are SoWiFa, DaHuFa, SoWiMo, DaHuMo. Marriage with one of these would turn ego's So and SoWi, Da and DaHu into stepbrothers and stepsisters, which would be most awkward.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1273
42723453db79,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,SoWiMo,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Among the affines ego must not marry are SoWiFa, DaHuFa, SoWiMo, DaHuMo. Marriage with one of these would turn ego's So and SoWi, Da and DaHu into stepbrothers and stepsisters, which would be most awkward.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1275
eafa964d26e9,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,Tũn!ga w.s.,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,allows joking,Tũn!ga w.s.,/san_marshall_217_sv:p::/san_marshall_217_sv::Tũn!ga w.s. allows joking; tũn!ga m.s. does not.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_217_sv:p,1224
f2780b0f3709,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,WiBr,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Marriage is prohibited with HuSiHu and WiBrWi, termed respectively ≠tum and / utsu; ego avoids joking with them as he avoids joking with HuSi and WiBr.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1280
d72ff2eeb608,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,WiBrWi,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,/ utsu,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Marriage is prohibited with HuSiHu and WiBrWi, termed respectively ≠tum and / utsu; ego avoids joking with them as he avoids joking with HuSi and WiBr.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1278
aeca7d1bf8de,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,WiBrWi,person,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,avoidance / constrained from joking,,"/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_342_1959_sv::In the sibling category among affines ego is prohibited from marrying only WiBrWi or HuSiHu. ... As we list ego's siblings and affines in Fig. 4 we see that WiBrWi and HuSiHu are the only ones whose sex is opposite to ego's, making marriage possible, but with whom ego is constrained from joking because he does not joke with his WiBr or HuSi, according the same joking status to both members of a married couple.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p,1313
5faf26b58442,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,WiSiDa,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_256_sv:p::/san_marshall_256_sv::Why, we had asked, is marriage with WiSiDa and HuBrSo specifically prohibited? ≠Toma explained that a man often marries his WiSi if his wife should die, or as a second wife. His being her potential husband makes him “feel like” her husband even though he is not married to her.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_256_sv:p,1269
f6275f0a1df3,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,WiSiHu,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,,"/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_342_1959_sv::Throughout the whole system (except among remote name relatives), ego maintains the same joking status with both members of a married couple, for example, with FaBr and FaBrWi, WiSi and WiSiHu, &c.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_342_1959_sv:p,1312
33242ad65162,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,adjacent generation,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::1) Avoidance relationship is applied to the adjacent generation, except for mother's brother, father's sister, and their spouses.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1387
4e0a5e503ba6,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,affines,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking status with affines,mi twisi,"/san_marshall_214_sv:p::/san_marshall_214_sv::A !Kung calls his affines mi twisi.

Once established, an affinal relationship is considered to be indissoluble even though the person through whom the relationship with ego was brought about be dead or divorced. For example, should ego's brother die, his brother's wife remains in affinal relationship with ego, and the application of a kin term and the joking status with her continue to be the same as if ego's brother were alive.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_214_sv:p,1214
8e5619c7f4b6,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,alternate generations,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::3) Joking relationship is applied to the persons belonging to the alternate generations.,0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1395
e8ea6de7f58a,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,anyone who has the name of his parents or offspring,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,name-relative (parent/offspring name),,/san_marshall_259_sv:p::/san_marshall_259_sv::The fourth category comprises certain name-relatives. Ego should not marry (1) anyone who has the name of his parents or offspring;,0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_259_sv:p,1284
5c0d029dfc5c,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,anyone who has the same name as ego's spouse's parent or ego's son's or daughter's spouse,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,name-relative (spouse's parent/child's spouse name),,/san_marshall_259_sv:p::/san_marshall_259_sv::Ego should not marry (3) anyone who has the same name as ego's spouse's parent or ego's son's or daughter's spouse.,0.75,0.75,1,1,/san_marshall_259_sv:p,1286
c8426afffb11,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,aunts,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::Ego avoids joking with his uncles, aunts, nephews, and nieces, who are, respectively, of his parents' and his offspring's generations.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1172
364ca7ab4877,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,brother's wife,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking status with brother's wife,,"/san_marshall_214_sv:p::/san_marshall_214_sv::For example, should ego's brother die, his brother's wife remains in affinal relationship with ego, and the application of a kin term and the joking status with her continue to be the same as if ego's brother were alive.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_214_sv:p,1215
a6536a856949,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,cousins,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::He jokes with his cousins, who are of his generation. || /san_marshall_208_sv:p::/san_marshall_208_sv::He considers ... his cousins to be “like” himself.",0.925,0.95,2,2,/san_marshall_206_sv:p; /san_marshall_208_sv:p,1175;1195
9e1abd333d23,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,cousins named for ego's parents,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,"tsu, //ga","/san_marshall_228_sv:p::/san_marshall_228_sv::Cousins would be termed !gun!a or tũn by the generational method; however, if they are named for ego's parents, the terms applied must be tsu or //ga.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_228_sv:p,1246
ba603ad515ef,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,cross-cousins,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking category,,"/san_silberbauer_311_1972_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_311_1972_sv::There are some situations in which it does not operate, for example, both cross-cousins and their parents are in the joking category, but this is changed if ego marries his cross-cousin, in which case the latter's parents are transferred to the avoidance category.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_silberbauer_311_1972_sv:p,1365
b0a8483c88dc,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,"ego's grandparents, same-sex siblings, opposite-sex cross cousins, and parents' opposite-sex siblings",kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_tanaka_105_sv:p::/san_tanaka_105_sv::Within the joking category, particularly free relations hold between ego and ego's grandparents, same-sex siblings, opposite-sex cross cousins, and parents' opposite-sex siblings, to the extent that they may exchange gossip and criticism about others, tell sexual stories, play pranks on each other, and so on.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_tanaka_105_sv:p,1409
55f5178f11af,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,father's sister,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::1) Avoidance relationship is applied to the adjacent generation, except for mother's brother, father's sister, and their spouses.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1389
b4b908203c5d,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,grandchildren,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::He jokes with his grandparents and his grandchildren, who are in generations alternate to the generation of his parents and offspring.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1177
18601a023ba5,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,grandparents,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::He jokes with his grandparents and his grandchildren, who are in generations alternate to the generation of his parents and offspring.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1176
229d5873905b,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,great-grandchildren,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_208_sv:p::/san_marshall_208_sv::Only among ego's lineal kin in the generation of great-grandparents, grandparents, grandchildren, great-grandchildren is the joking relation established by the generational method.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_208_sv:p,1199
4934a1513a96,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,great-grandparents,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_208_sv:p::/san_marshall_208_sv::Only among ego's lineal kin in the generation of great-grandparents, grandparents, grandchildren, great-grandchildren is the joking relation established by the generational method.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_208_sv:p,1196
564b23070c4c,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,his own offspring,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_207_sv:p::/san_marshall_207_sv::They said that just as they must not joke with their own parents or offspring, they must not joke with both a person and that person's offspring.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_207_sv:p,1190
2d177db61e97,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,his own parents,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_207_sv:p::/san_marshall_207_sv::They said that just as they must not joke with their own parents or offspring, they must not joke with both a person and that person's offspring.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_207_sv:p,1189
a0bffd473a80,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,male named for ego,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,"!Gun!a, !guma","/san_marshall_228_sv:p::/san_marshall_228_sv::!Gun!a is the term used for a male named for himself; but the term would be in its diminutive form, !guma. A male named for ego would be younger than ego. That male would reciprocate by calling ego !gun!a.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_228_sv:p,1245
b38a4dc4409e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,members of the nuclear family and certain consanguineous relatives,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_340_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_340_1959_sv::And, although they must not direct sexual jokes or insults to each other, they may laugh as heartily when they overhear the jokes as relatives do who have the joking relationship together.
The !Kung use the expression ‘We are one people’ when they refer to certain consanguineous relatives—e.g. any lineal kin and the close collaterals listed in Fig. 2",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_340_1959_sv:p,1304
90f7508c0c59,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,mother's brother,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::1) Avoidance relationship is applied to the adjacent generation, except for mother's brother, father's sister, and their spouses.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1388
1195a37e04e0,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,n!unba,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,allows joking,n!unba,"/san_marshall_217_sv:p::/san_marshall_217_sv::As to the joking relationship: !hoa, tsau, n!unba, and n!untai allow joking; ≠tum and /utsu do not.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_217_sv:p,1222
