fecc8fd953eb,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,name relatives classified as grandparents,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,may joke,name relationship,"/san_marshall_343_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_343_1959_sv::They may joke with name relatives whose names classify them with grandparents, a sibling of the same sex, or the spouse.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_343_1959_sv:p,1315
204df6add0fe,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,name relatives classified as the spouse,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,may joke,name relationship,"/san_marshall_343_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_343_1959_sv::They may joke with name relatives whose names classify them with grandparents, a sibling of the same sex, or the spouse.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_343_1959_sv:p,1317
d729954b5d6d,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,nephews,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::Ego avoids joking with his uncles, aunts, nephews, and nieces, who are, respectively, of his parents' and his offspring's generations.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1173
19bbadd92447,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,nephews and nieces (kin likened to offspring generation),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,joking allowed with kin likened to offspring generation,,"/san_marshall_341_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_341_1959_sv::Siblings of parents are ‘like’ parents, cousins are ‘like’ siblings, nephews and nieces are ‘like’ offspring. ... Joking is allowed or not as it is with ego's kin in these generations.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_341_1959_sv:p,1306
e6d3dd648185,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,nephews and nieces named for ego's parents,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,"tsu, //ga","/san_marshall_228_sv:p::/san_marshall_228_sv::Some of ego's nephews and nieces would be named for ego's parents. ... The generational terms which have the same generational association and joking status as the terms for parents and offspring are tsu and //ga, and these are the terms ego uses for relatives named for his parents and offspring.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_228_sv:p,1243
fa9c2c1be8a2,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,nieces,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::Ego avoids joking with his uncles, aunts, nephews, and nieces, who are, respectively, of his parents' and his offspring's generations.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1174
9e0a2319d39c,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,offspring,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,_koa,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::In the nuclear family, ego avoids joking with his parents and his offspring.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1166
7edccc248eac,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,offspring's spouse's parents,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,,/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::His offspring's spouse's parents are like himself; he jokes with them.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1179
9f0bf77b880e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,offspring's spouses,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,,/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::His offspring's spouses are like his offspring; he avoids joking.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1180
13324f326456,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,parallel cousin of the opposite sex,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::2) Joking relationship is applied to the same generation, except siblings of the opposite sex, parallel cousin of the opposite sex, and their spouses.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1393
bd39d6956cd7,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,parents,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,_koa,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::In the nuclear family, ego avoids joking with his parents and his offspring.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1165
50707f86dd73,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,parents of ego's SoWi and DaHu,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,may joke with (affines),,"/san_marshall_341_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_341_1959_sv::Parents of ego's SoWi and DaHu are terminologically of ego's generation and he may joke with them but he must not marry them, for that would make his Regulation Of Marriage So and SoWi or Da and DaHu stepbrother and stepsister to each other, which would be most awkward.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_341_1959_sv:p,1307
e4cee44d6ed0,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,parents' siblings,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_208_sv:p::/san_marshall_208_sv::What a !Kung says, when he associates his relatives with each other in the pattern I have called generational, is that they are “like” each other. He considers his parents' siblings to be “like” his parents, ... Instead it was the joking relationship they spoke of, and they pointed out the parallel position of their kin in its terms.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_208_sv:p,1193
c05af5b636e6,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,person for whom he is named,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,!gun!a usage,!gun!a,"/san_marshall_229_sv:p::/san_marshall_229_sv::The term !gun!a has other applications. Ego applied it to the person for whom he is named, and also to anyone, related or not, who happens to have the same name as his, and to relatives named for him—with two exceptions:",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_229_sv:p,1248
2630c11631af,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,persons named for ego's spouse,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,"!gun!a, tũn!ga, tũn","/san_marshall_229_sv:p::/san_marshall_229_sv::The terms applied to persons named for ego's spouse are also !gun!a (or tũn!ga w.s.) or tũn. The affinal terms !hoa and tsau for husband and wife are used only for ego's actual spouse. Persons named for the spouse, who is terminologically of ego's generation, have the generational terms applied to them that classify them with ego's generation and give them the joking relationship.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_229_sv:p,1247
256f36165c55,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,persons termed !gu!na (or tun!ga w.s.),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,!gu!na; tun!ga w.s.,/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_19_1957_sv::The preferred marriage among !Kung is with a non-consanguineous name-relative whom ego terms !gu!na (or tun!ga w.s.) or tũn m.s.,0.7,0.7,1,1,/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p,1153
ce29729a30eb,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,persons termed //ga,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,//ga,/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_19_1957_sv::Persons who use the terms tsu and //ga for each other may marry unless one has the name of the other's parent.,0.6,0.6,1,1,/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p,1156
e74476a88408,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,persons termed sibling terms,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_19_1957_sv::Persons who use the sibling terms may marry. These marriages, though not forbidden, are not preferred.",0.5,0.5,1,1,/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p,1157
0aabbbc1ad61,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,persons termed tsu,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,tsu,"/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_19_1957_sv::Sometimes an informant would not know whether, for instance, a relative he termed tsu was his FaBr, his MoBr or who, but would say that his parents taught him to use that term for the relative and that he must not joke with him.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p,1155
13821202a8fc,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,persons termed tũn m.s.,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,,tũn m.s.,/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p::/san_marshall_19_1957_sv::The preferred marriage among !Kung is with a non-consanguineous name-relative whom ego terms !gu!na (or tun!ga w.s.) or tũn m.s.,0.7,0.7,1,1,/san_marshall_19_1957_sv:p,1154
1a2c01a9e6f7,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,relatives named for another of ego's kin,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_229_sv:p::/san_marshall_229_sv::When some relative is named for another of ego's kin, ego applies the same term to him that he applied to the kinsman.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_229_sv:p,1250
61929fd06185,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,relatives named for ego's sibling,person,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_228_sv:p::/san_marshall_228_sv::If a relative is named for ego's sibling, ego applies sibling terms to the relative, and ego has the same joking position with him that he would have with his sibling.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_marshall_228_sv:p,1244
afb082b291d5,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,relatives named for him,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relationship,!gun!a,"/san_marshall_229_sv:p::/san_marshall_229_sv::Ego applied it to the person for whom he is named, and also to anyone, related or not, who happens to have the same name as his, and to relatives named for him—with two exceptions:",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_229_sv:p,1249
76ae3c2f6f6b,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,same generation,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::2) Joking relationship is applied to the same generation, except siblings of the opposite sex, parallel cousin of the opposite sex, and their spouses.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1391
8ba3dd77bd38,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,sibling of the same sex,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,jokes with,,/san_marshall_217_sv:p::/san_marshall_217_sv::Ego jokes with a sibling of the same sex and with the spouse of that sibling.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_217_sv:p,1225
bb7cc1392476,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,sibling's offspring,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_208_sv:p::/san_marshall_208_sv::He considers his parents' siblings to be “like” his parents, his sibling's offspring to be “like” his offspring, his cousins to be “like” himself.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_208_sv:p,1194
1c7c6280db5b,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,siblings of parents (kin likened to parents' generation),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,joking allowed with kin likened to parents' generation,,"/san_marshall_341_1959_sv:p::/san_marshall_341_1959_sv::The kin who are likened, by being of the same generation, to his parents, to his offspring, and to his siblings, are those to whom a !Kung feels the marriage Regulation Of Marriage regulations are particularly directed. ... Joking is allowed or not as it is with ego's kin in these generations.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_341_1959_sv:p,1305
951f39cd4c5e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,siblings of the opposite sex,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::2) Joking relationship is applied to the same generation, except siblings of the opposite sex, parallel cousin of the opposite sex, and their spouses.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1392
ec0d2393694c,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,spouse of that sibling,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,jokes with,,/san_marshall_217_sv:p::/san_marshall_217_sv::Ego jokes with a sibling of the same sex and with the spouse of that sibling.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_217_sv:p,1226
71c1a6c6f24e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,spouse's parents,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,_koa,/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::Affines fall into a similar pattern. Ego's spouse's parents are like his parents; ego avoids joking with them.,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1178
d146812ae7d4,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,"the parent, offspring, or sibling of opposite sex of anyone who has the same name as ego",kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,name-relative (relatives of same-name person),,"/san_marshall_259_sv:p::/san_marshall_259_sv::Ego should not marry (2) the parent, offspring, or sibling of opposite sex of anyone who has the same name as ego;",0.75,0.75,1,1,/san_marshall_259_sv:p,1285
084ee28b781a,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,their spouses,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::1) Avoidance relationship is applied to the adjacent generation, except for mother's brother, father's sister, and their spouses.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1390
a75c866fb381,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,their spouses,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,symmetric,,,"/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p::/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv::2) Joking relationship is applied to the same generation, except siblings of the opposite sex, parallel cousin of the opposite sex, and their spouses.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_sugawara_25_1984_sv:p,1394
cdca10cdc2dd,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,tsu,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,tsu (avoidance),tsu,"/san_marshall_221_sv:p::/san_marshall_221_sv::The terms !gun!a and tũn are applied to the persons with whom ego may joke, tsu and //ga to persons with whom he avoids joking.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_221_sv:p,1235
d7ab97ab2088,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,tuma (younger than ego),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relation; relaxed joking relation,tuma,"/san_lee_358_1972_sv:p::/san_lee_358_1972_sv::The tuns and tumas are the girls with whom ego has a relaxed joking relation, the female equivalent of the cordial “old name—young name” relation. || /san_lee_367_sv:p::/san_lee_367_sv::tun (older than ego) and tuma (younger than ego): kin terms for females; these are females with whom ego has a joking relation",0.925,0.95,2,2,/san_lee_358_1972_sv:p; /san_lee_367_sv:p,1149;1151
5ee5af99987e,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,tun (older than ego),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relation,tun,/san_lee_367_sv:p::/san_lee_367_sv::tun (older than ego) and tuma (younger than ego): kin terms for females; these are females with whom ego has a joking relation,0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_lee_367_sv:p,1150
1b1c723b1eae,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,tun (older),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,relaxed joking relation,tun,"/san_lee_358_1972_sv:p::/san_lee_358_1972_sv::The tuns and tumas are the girls with whom ego has a relaxed joking relation, the female equivalent of the cordial “old name—young name” relation.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/san_lee_358_1972_sv:p,1148
2c3f71e143ca,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,tũn,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,tũn (joking),tũn,"/san_marshall_221_sv:p::/san_marshall_221_sv::The terms !gun!a and tũn are applied to the persons with whom ego may joke, tsu and //ga to persons with whom he avoids joking.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/san_marshall_221_sv:p,1234
a51eda981a27,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,uncles,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::Ego avoids joking with his uncles, aunts, nephews, and nieces, who are, respectively, of his parents' and his offspring's generations.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1171
e464a3317eff,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,elder brother,younger brother,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_silberbauer_165_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_165_sv::Consistent with this vicarious authority, the relationship between same-sex siblings before the younger attains independent status is a mixture of joking and respect.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_165_sv:p,1352
158ecd9f6278,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,elder sister,younger sister,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_silberbauer_165_sv:p::/san_silberbauer_165_sv::Consistent with this vicarious authority, the relationship between same-sex siblings before the younger attains independent status is a mixture of joking and respect.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_silberbauer_165_sv:p,1353
b600d4f4ab95,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,female,brother,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::Among siblings, according to a cross and parallel pattern in which a sex differentiation is made, a ... female jokes with her sister, but not with her brother.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1170
6266a46af25f,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,female,sister,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,,"/san_marshall_206_sv:p::/san_marshall_206_sv::Among siblings, according to a cross and parallel pattern in which a sex differentiation is made, a ... female jokes with her sister, but not with her brother.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/san_marshall_206_sv:p,1169
268e92185a4d,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,female ego,BrWiBr,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,joking with BrWiBr,!gun!a / tũn!ga,"/san_marshall_221_sv:p::/san_marshall_221_sv::A female ego would avoid joking with BrWiSi since she does not joke with BrWi, and to her BrWiSi she would apply the term //ga-n!untai; she would take the opposite position with BrWiBr, whom she would term !gun!a- (or tũn!ga-) n!unba.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_221_sv:p,1240
05b53be49d90,within_group,SouthernAfrica,san,female ego,BrWiSi,kin_role,kin_role,avoidance,unclear,avoidance with BrWiSi,//ga-n!untai,"/san_marshall_221_sv:p::/san_marshall_221_sv::A female ego would avoid joking with BrWiSi since she does not joke with BrWi, and to her BrWiSi she would apply the term //ga-n!untai; she would take the opposite position with BrWiBr, whom she would term !gun!a- (or tũn!ga-) n!unba.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/san_marshall_221_sv:p,1239
