19b365e337f7,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,a woman,her older sibling’s spouse,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking,,"/Hausa_Greenberg_204_NK:p::/Hausa_Greenberg_204_NK::The other joking relationships between individuals are between grandparents and grandchildren, between parents and their youngest child (who in this as in other respects is assimilated to a grandchild), between a man and his older sibling’s spouse and a woman and her older sibling’s spouse.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Greenberg_204_NK:p,641
674bbcd79ad8,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,a younger brother of a husband or wife,husband or wife,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,abokin wasa,Abokin wasa,"/Hausa_Hill_203_NK:p::/Hausa_Hill_203_NK::Abokin wasa. The ‘joking-relationship’ between certain friends, occupational groups, and categories of kin, the latter including cross-cousins, grandparents (and grandchildren) and a younger brother of a husband or wife.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/Hausa_Hill_203_NK:p,649
f0cb7107990d,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,abokan wasa (cross-cousins and grandparents) of a spouse,his partner by marriage,group,person,joking_relationship,unclear,abokan wasa,abokan wasa,"/Hausa_Smith_44_NK:p::/Hausa_Smith_44_NK::Joking relationships between the spouses of Ego’s elder siblings of different sex and Ego, and also between the abokan wasa (cross-cousins and grandparents, particularly the former) of a spouse and his partner by marriage, tend to relieve the tensions inherent in affinal relationships and the conditions of Hausa marriage.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/Hausa_Smith_44_NK:p,675
715ecf9e02cf,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,barber-doctors (wanzamai),blacksmiths (makira),caste,caste,joking_relationship,symmetric,,"wanzamai, makira","/Hausa_Smith_43_NK:p::/Hausa_Smith_43_NK::barber-doctors and blacksmiths (wanzamai, makira);",0.95,0.95,1,1,/Hausa_Smith_43_NK:p,667
5e032dd71c98,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,bride,bridegroom’s younger sister,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,mixed,bride’s new joking relation,,"/Hausa_Baba_94_NK:p::/Hausa_Baba_94_NK::Then the groom’s younger sister, the bride’s new joking relation, comes quickly with a vessel of water with a threepanny piece in it, she puts it down at the Life History Materials door of the hut and runs away.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Baba_94_NK:p,615
391af5fe7d1f,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,bride,the bride's girl-friends,kin_role,group,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,,,"/Hausa_Baba_93_NK:p::/Hausa_Baba_93_NK::Then it is the turn of the bride’s girl-friends to prevent her from entering her hut, they sing and the chief kawa hangs onto the bride.",0.85,0.85,1,1,/Hausa_Baba_93_NK:p,614
1e2bb9f74395,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,bride,the bridegroom’s grandmothers,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,unclear,new joking relations,,"/Hausa_Baba_93_NK:p::/Hausa_Baba_93_NK::But when they arrive at her hut door they find her new joking relations, the bridegroom’s grandmothers, sitting there and saying that they can’t come in with the bride! When they are given a little money they get up and let her in.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Baba_93_NK:p,612
209c4d372c79,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,bride’s kawa,bridegroom’s younger sisters,group,kin_role,joking_relationship,mixed,playing and teasing,,"/Hausa_Baba_94_NK:p::/Hausa_Baba_94_NK::The bride’s friends and the groom’s younger sisters are playing and teasing, the friends won’t let the bridegroom’s younger sisters enter the bride’s hut, and when food is being eaten, if the younger sisters come near, the bride’s friends will smear them with porridge and stew and oil and they will have to run away and wash.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Baba_94_NK:p,616
95df90acad0b,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,brothers-in-law,sisters-in-law,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking / play,,"/Hausa_Greenberg_204_NK:p::/Hausa_Greenberg_204_NK::Grandparents and grandchildren of opposite sex call each other “husband” and “wife” in play, and this is also true of brothers-in-law and sisters-in-law who are joking relatives.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/Hausa_Greenberg_204_NK:p,642
14660e0f6d0b,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,butchers (mahauta),blacksmiths (makira),caste,caste,joking_relationship,symmetric,,"mahauta, makira","/Hausa_Smith_43_NK:p::/Hausa_Smith_43_NK::It is to be noted that joking relationships are not [unavailable] to kin and affines, but also hold on set occasions between categories or persons of different occupation, affiliation with an ethnic group, or state, thus: butchers and blacksmiths (mahauta, makira),",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Smith_43_NK:p,665
ffe97b8c1a50,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,certain friends,certain friends,group,group,joking_relationship,symmetric,abokin wasa,Abokin wasa,"/Hausa_Hill_203_NK:p::/Hausa_Hill_203_NK::Abokin wasa. The ‘joking-relationship’ between certain friends, occupational groups, and categories of kin, the latter including cross-cousins, grandparents (and grandchildren) and a younger brother of a husband or wife.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Hill_203_NK:p,645
10ef03f43637,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,child of the female sibling,child of the male sibling,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,cross-cousin jokingrelationship,,"/Hausa_Smith_44_NK:p::/Hausa_Smith_44_NK::The bilateral cross-cousin jokingrelationship which is expressed by the collection of kudin shara at the Mohammedan New Year, the child of the female sibling claiming ½d. or 1d. from the child of the male sibling because, as Hausa say, “the son of the male is the slave of the son of the female”.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/Hausa_Smith_44_NK:p,673
3aaace3c153b,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,children,grandparents,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,privileged teasing,,"/Hausa_Baba_21_NK:p::/Hausa_Baba_21_NK::Joking relationships, expressed by privileged behaviour such as teasing, and the right to appropriate certain possessions of the other party, obtain between children and their grandparents, ... the first-named parties being privileged to tease and take things from the last-named, who retaliate with good-natured abuse and more teasing.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Baba_21_NK:p,605
f03861d060d4,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,children of a sister,children of a brother,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,privileged teasing,,"/Hausa_Baba_21_NK:p::/Hausa_Baba_21_NK::Joking relationships, expressed by privileged behaviour such as teasing, and the right to appropriate certain possessions of the other party, obtain between children and their grandparents, and between children of a sister and a brother, in both cases the first-named parties being privileged to tease and take things from the last-named, who retaliate with good-natured abuse and more teasing.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Baba_21_NK:p,606
