9db806cadd13,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,cross-cousins,cross-cousins,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,abokin wasa,Abokin wasa,"/Hausa_Hill_203_NK:p::/Hausa_Hill_203_NK::Abokin wasa. The ‘joking-relationship’ between certain friends, occupational groups, and categories of kin, the latter including cross-cousins, grandparents (and grandchildren) and a younger brother of a husband or wife. || /Hausa_Smith_46_NK:p::/Hausa_Smith_46_NK::In both the Fulani and Hausa kinship systems, cross-cousins are joking relations whose relationship involves privileged familiarity.",0.925,0.95,2,2,/Hausa_Hill_203_NK:p; /Hausa_Smith_46_NK:p,647;683
