6237e223e719,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,cross-cousins,each other,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,’abó[unknown]kán wa[unknown]sá[unknown] (playmates),’abó[unknown]kán wa[unknown]sá[unknown],"/Hausa_Greenberg_203_NK:p::/Hausa_Greenberg_203_NK::Although the kinship terminology, which is in general of the merging type, gives no special recognition to cross- cousins as opposed to parallel cousins, cross cousins, whether of the same or opposite sex, are said to be ’abó[unknown]kán wa[unknown]sá[unknown], “playmates.”",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Greenberg_203_NK:p,634
51f0f10a9378,within_group,WesternAfrica,Hausa,dimajo,"his master's children, real and classificatory ('yanuwa)",kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,joking relations,,"/Hausa_Smith_253_NK:p::/Hausa_Smith_253_NK::he was from birth incorporated in the Muhammadan population, and addressed his master as father ( baba ); his master’s children, real and classificatory, were his siblings (’ yanuwa ), and some of  them were his joking relations.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/Hausa_Smith_253_NK:p,656
