4fec58b62d89,within_group,WesternAfrica,wolof,child of the mother9s brother,child of the father9s sister,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,mixed,master/slave (borom/jam) joking relationship,"borom, jam","/wolof_47_nk:p::/wolof_47_nk::Like many other peoples, the Wolof have an institution-alized cross cousins relationship. It is especially marked by a jokingrelationship between the child Regulation Of of the mother9s brother who is called ""master"" ( borom) and the child of the father9s sister who is called ""slave"" ( jam).",0.9,0.9,1,1,/wolof_47_nk:p,1489
4585698d397e,within_group,WesternAfrica,wolof,grandfathers,grandsons,kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,jokingrelationship,,"/wolof_35_nk:p::/wolof_35_nk::There is a jokingrelationship between grandfathers and grandsons. A grandson is permitted to act disrespectfully toward his grandfather, pulling his beard, calling him by a nickname, making fun of his physique, and contradicting him.",0.9,0.9,1,1,/wolof_35_nk:p,1488
02cf915043bf,within_group,WesternAfrica,wolof,jam (father's sister's child),b[unknown]r[unknown]m (mother's brother's child),kin_role,kin_role,joking_relationship,symmetric,,jam / b[unknown]r[unknown]m,"/wolof_55_nk:p::/wolof_55_nk::Among the Wolof the relationship is expressed in terms of jam (slave) and b[unknown]r[unknown]m (master), a father’s sister’s child will be jam, a mother's brother’s child b[unknown]r[unknown]m. On ceremonial occasions the jam come to help their b[unknown]r[unknown]m, and are rewarded for their services.",0.95,0.95,1,1,/wolof_55_nk:p,1490
cb79598e481b,within_group,WesternAfrica,wolof,men,younger women,group,group,joking_relationship,non_symmetric,take liberties / joke with,,"/wolof_98_nk:p::/wolof_98_nk::A man does not give an older woman such consideration, though he will not joke with her or take other liberties as he does with younger women.",0.8,0.8,1,1,/wolof_98_nk:p,1494
